.\" tmo(1) manual page
.TH TMO 1 "September 2026" "tmo-cli 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmo \- headless CLI client for DIGITS from T-Mobile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmo
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmo
authenticates to DIGITS (T-Mobile's line-sharing service) via the real
browser OAuth flow, then operates the line over the DaaS REST API and the
WRG WebSocket notification protocol: sending texts, reading call history,
checking voicemail, placing voice calls, running an AI text auto-responder,
and bridging calls to an OpenAI GPT-Live voice agent.
.PP
Authentication is browser-login-only: credentials are obtained exclusively
through \fBtmo login\fR (browser + 2FA + localhost:8080 callback). There is
no REST token refresh by design — the scripted path trips bot detection.
Access tokens live ~24h.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login [\-\-username N]
Browser OAuth login (password + SMS 2FA). Saves tokens to
.IR tokens.json .
With \-\-username (10 digits), non-interactive credential entry.
.TP
.B register
Establish the DaaS session and register this device on the line
(\fImanageSession\fR then \fIregister\fR — the app's order).
.TP
.B status
Show device identity, line, and token state.
.TP
.B sms send \-\-to N \-\-text T
Send a text from the line to a 10-digit number. Rides the RCS/IMS chat
stack when the recipient is capable (delivery + read receipts).
.TP
.B threads
List conversation threads (device-scoped: a fresh device sees only
messages from its connection onward).
.TP
.B calllogs
Line-scoped call history: numbers, direction, duration, timestamps.
.TP
.B e911
E911 address on file for the line.
.TP
.B listen
Live monitor: connect the notification channel and print every incoming
text/call/registration event as it happens.
.TP
.B respond
AI auto-responder: texts arriving from the allowlisted number
(\fBTMO_RESPOND_TO\fR in .env) are answered by OpenAI gpt-5.4-mini using
the mission prompt in \fIlib/respond_persona.txt\fR. All other senders
are logged and ignored. Requires \fBOAI_API_KEY\fR.
.TP
.B call \-\-target N [\-\-hold S]
Place a voice call (WebRTC, PCMU/opus). Requires the \fBvoice\fR extra.
.TP
.B ai-call \-\-target N [\-\-max S]
AI voice agent holds the call via OpenAI GPT-Live. Requires \fBvoice\fR
and \fBai\fR extras and \fBOAI_API_KEY\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .env
Credentials: TMOBILE_USERNAME, TMOBILE_PASSWORD, OAI_API_KEY,
TMO_RESPOND_TO. Never committed.
.TP
.I tokens.json
DaaS tokens from the last \fBtmo login\fR.
.TP
.I device.json
This install's device identity (UUID + session number).
.SH SECURITY
The DIGITS API accepts a single \fIdaasAccessToken\fR header with no
client attestation, and the desktop app stores it unencrypted. Any
process on the machine can operate the line. This tool demonstrates that
exposure — use only on your own account. Rapid automated call attempts
can trigger carrier fraud throttling (403 CC_TRANS_O_FRAUDULENT_MOBILE);
if calls suddenly fail, stop for 24–48h.
.SH INSTALL
.B pip install git+https://github.com/TravelMaxx/tmo-cli.git
.br
.B curl \-fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TravelMaxx/tmo-cli/main/quick-install.sh | bash
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: \fIhttps://github.com/TravelMaxx/tmo-cli\fR
